MoBL-ARMS Dynamic Upper Limb Model
==================================

Source: https://github.com/CEINMS-RT/UpperLimbModel (MOBL_ARMS_41.osim)
Upstream project: https://simtk.org/projects/upexdyn/

License: non-commercial BSD 3-Clause (see LICENSE excerpt in README.md of this
folder / upstream). Commercial use requires a separate license from the
copyright holders.

Required citations when using the model:
  Saul KR, Hu X, Goehler CM, Daly M, Vidt ME, Velisar A, Murray WM.
  Benchmarking of dynamic simulation predictions in two software platforms
  using an upper limb musculoskeletal model. CMBBE. 2015; 18:1445-58.

  McFarland DC, McCain EM, Poppo MN, Saul KR. Spatial Dependency of
  Glenohumeral Joint Stability During Dynamic Unimanual and Bimanual
  Pushing and Pulling. ASME J Biomech Eng. 2019; 141(5): 051006.

Integration note (CeRebel):
  MoBL-ARMS is a right upper-extremity model with clavicle/scapula DOFs.
  It is NOT a drop-in replacement for Rajagopal full-body. CeRebel keeps
  Rajagopal(+neck) as the primary IK skeleton and optionally drives MoBL
  from solved arm poses to export upper-limb musculotendon path polylines
  for visualization alongside Rajagopal lower-limb muscles.
